# Graphly (`kb` commands)

Users type git-style commands in chat. Call the matching Graphly MCP tool.

## Vocabulary

| User says | MCP tool |
|-----------|----------|
| `kb list` | `kb_list` |
| `kb create <id> [name]` | `kb_create` |
| `kb use <id>` | write `.cursor/kb-id` (no MCP call) |
| `kb push <text>` | `kb_push` |
| `kb fetch <question>` | `kb_fetch` |
| `kb invite <email> [read\|write]` | `kb_invite` |
| `kb members` | `kb_members` |
| `kb revoke <email>` | `kb_revoke` |
| `kb delete <id>` | `kb_delete` |

Also accept natural language that clearly means the same thing
(e.g. "push this to the knowledge base", "fetch what DB we use").

## Defaults

- Prefer `kb_id` from `.cursor/kb-id`.
- If missing and required, call `kb_list` or ask.
- `kb_push` always needs a fresh UUID `idempotency_key`.

## Auto behavior

- Before architecture / "what did we decide" answers → `kb_fetch`.
- When the user states a durable decision to keep → offer or run `kb_push`.

## Do not

- Invent memories that were not fetched.
- Confuse OAuth identity with `.cursor/kb-id` (kb-id is only which graph).
